 "notes": "OSQAR light-shining-through-wall experiment (2014 run, 9 T x 2x14.3 m, 18.5 W 532 nm laser). Curve is the 95% CL pseudoscalar ALP (E||B) exclusion from Fig. 6, extracted from the vector paths of the e-print file OsqarPaper2014_fig6.pdf; axis calibration verified against tick marks and the quoted flat limit g_Agamma < 3.5e-8 GeV^-1 for m_A < 2e-4 eV (extracted flat value 3.46-3.50e-8). The paper also reports a scalar ALP (E perp B) limit of 3.2e-8 GeV^-1; the pseudoscalar curve is reported here as the axion-photon result. Couplings at the sinc-lobe spikes that exit the top of the plotted frame are clamped at the frame top (2.0e-6 GeV^-1). Laboratory LSW bound: no dark-matter density assumption, no rescaling applied.",
